Subject: [PATCH 1/7] platforms.json: add the Microsoft Surface Laptop 7

Exact DMI match. The installer installs linux-sl7 next to the stock
linux-aarch64 rescue kernel; the packages come from the local [omarchy-sl7]
repository, and linux-firmware-qcom from ALARM.

diff --git a/configs/aarch64/platforms.json b/configs/aarch64/platforms.json
index 0c903a5..6bbb201 100644
--- a/configs/aarch64/platforms.json
+++ b/configs/aarch64/platforms.json
@@ -11,6 +11,22 @@
       "packages": ["linux-firmware-qcom"],
       "kernel_cmdline": []
     },
+    {
+      "id": "microsoft-surface-laptop-7",
+      "name": "Microsoft Surface Laptop 7",
+      "media_target": "aarch64/snapdragon",
+      "match": [
+        { "sys_vendor": "Microsoft Corporation", "product_name": "Microsoft Surface Laptop, 7th Edition" }
+      ],
+      "packages": [
+        "linux-sl7",
+        "linux-sl7-headers",
+        "omarchy-surface-sl7",
+        "iptsd-sl7",
+        "linux-firmware-qcom"
+      ],
+      "kernel_cmdline": []
+    },
     {
       "id": "nvidia-dgx-spark",
       "name": "NVIDIA DGX Spark",
